  "description": "Ghogalo is a snail with a quirky face and a wooden rolling barrel for a shell. Inside the barrel children can run and roll, and an orange spiral marks the shell from outside. Antenna-shaped net climbers stand at the head and a wavy balance trail runs along the body. Children aged 5 to 12 use it, up to 15 at a time. The snail is long and slim, 31'1\" x 6'9\", with a safe play area of 35'1\" x 11'9\". Climbing, crawling, rolling, sitting and balancing build arm strength, hand-eye coordination and imaginative play. It is offered in Mineral and Royal Turquoise. Our 3-year warranty covers the galvanised pipes, roto-moulded parts, composite laminates and play rope. Call +91 902 830 2266 for a quote.",
